    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NNKdpkG3GKrYB8hHbRYuGq)_\n\n## Problem\n\n- `C-x b` did not offer `*Messages*` right after startup.\n- Cause: `tabspaces-use-filtered-buffers-as-default` remapped `switch-to-buffer` to a command listing only the tab's buffers, and `tabspaces-exclude-buffers` removes `*Messages*` from that list.\n\n## Change\n\n- `tabspaces-use-filtered-buffers-as-default` is now nil.\n- `C-x b` runs `sp-tabs-switch-to-buffer`, remapped in `tabspaces-mode-map`.\n- Default: the regular `switch-to-buffer` (all buffers, `*Messages*` included).\n- Filtered switcher (tab's buffers, then `*Messages*` at the end) applies when:\n  - `sp-tabs-filter-buffers` is non-nil (every tab), or\n  - the tab name is in `sp-tabs-filtered-tab-names` (default `\"Email\"`), or\n  - the major mode is derived from `sp-tabs-filtered-modes` (mu4e main/headers/view, `message-mode`).\n- `sp-tabs-toggle-tab-filter` toggles the current tab by name (`f` in `tabspaces-command-map`), meant for Projectile/project tabs.\n- `tabspaces-exclude-buffers` is unchanged.\n- Literate doc `docs/tangles/ui/sp-tabs.org` updated in step with the `.el`.\n\n## Tested in batch Emacs 29.3\n\n- [x] Remap resolves to `sp-tabs-switch-to-buffer`.\n- [x] Default tab runs the regular switcher.\n- [x] Tab named `Email` runs the filtered switcher; the toggle turns it off and on.\n- [x] Filtered candidates include `*Messages*` although the tab's list lacks it.\n\n## Not tested (no GUI)\n\n- Real startup with Vertico, Marginalia and the posframe minibuffer.\n- mu4e modes (mu4e not installed in the container).\n- Session restore interaction.\n\n## Manual testing checklist\n\n- [ ] Fresh start, `C-x b`: every buffer is listed, `*Messages*` included.\n- [ ] In the Email workspace (or a mu4e buffer), `C-x b` lists only that tab's buffers, `*Messages*` last.\n- [ ] In a project tab, run `sp-tabs-toggle-tab-filter` (`f` after the tabspaces prefix): the message says the filter is on, and `C-x b` shows only that project's buffers.\n- [ ] Run it again: the filter is off and all buffers are listed.\n- [ ] Marginalia annotations/icons still show in both modes.\n- [ ] `tabspaces-switch-to-buffer` called directly still works as before.\n- [ ] Closing a workspace does not kill `*Messages*`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiD9ebSHChd2mUbx219\n",
